,"text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for each iteration."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The unit’s work runs in the signal’s task each time iteration begins; a unit that fails"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends the batched sequence with its error. When the batched sequence ends first, the unit’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work is cancelled; a unit whose work ignores cancellation keeps the batch’s internal task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alive until it returns, though the batched sequence itself ends at once. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" takes "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/signal(_:)-88w9i","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves the subject alone. Each batched sequence iterated with this strategy runs the unit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anew and fires once when it completes."}]},{"anchor":"Example","level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let reachable = DeferredTask { try await server.waitUntilReachable() }","for try await requests in outbox.batch(strategy: .either(.count(20), .signal(reachable))) {","    try await send(requests)","}"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Type Method","symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyPAAE6signalyAA06SignalbC0Vyqd__AA14AsyncSequencesO8DeferredVy_Scsy7SuccessQyd_0_s5Error_pGGGqd_0_APRszAA22AsynchronousUnitOfWorkRd_0_r0_lFZ